+## Threads
+
+Every headless run is a thread of its project, in `~/.cedia/projects/<slug>/threads/<id>.jsonl`, append-only; the folded state is what `cedia threads` and the thread tools show. When a writer session's context passes `--handoff-at` (default half the window, at most 150k) and has doubled since its first reply, it writes a handoff note while its prefix is still cached; a new session of the thread starts from the task and the note. Nothing is edited, old logs stay searchable with `recall`, and the done gate still wants a check after inherited writes. `--thread <id>` goes on in the thread's last session when the model matches, otherwise in a new session from the latest note or result. Thread messages reach a session as a logged reminder at the next turn boundary.

